declare module.description:
TS 1.0
declare module 'name' { ... }
Provides ambient type declarations for a module that has none of its own (e.g. an untyped npm package) — usually placed in a `.d.ts` file.

declare global.description:
TS 2.8
declare global { ... }
Augments the global scope from inside a module file — e.g. adding a custom property to `Window`.
